    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #331\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-125-mcp-integration-04-07-synchronize-tool-thr_4925wmgiz3` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #125: \"Synchronize tools only on human request.\"\n\n- **`mcpSync.ts`** (new): `syncMcpServerTools` opens a connection through the #231 connection factory, calls `tools/list`, strictly validates the response (rejects blank or duplicate tool names), and transactionally materializes registrations into `mcp_tool_registrations` (#124):\n  - New tool names get the table's default `requires_approval=true`/`risk_class='unclassified'`.\n  - Existing human classification (risk class, approval) is preserved across a re-sync while schema/description refresh.\n  - Tools the server stops advertising become `active=false` rather than being deleted, preserving audit identity.\n  - Records `syncStatus`/`lastSynced`/`syncError` (all `owner: 'system'`, new schema fields) on the server item on both success and failure, using the safe-error shape from `McpConnectionError`/`ValidationError` — never a raw underlying message.\n  - The connection is always closed via `finally`, on both success and failure.\n  - Not exposed as any AgentTool/MCP operation — only reachable by an authenticated human caller.\n- Added `deactivateMcpToolRegistrationsNotIn` to `mcpToolRegistrationsStore.ts`.\n- Extended the shared #231 contract test servers (stdio/sse/http) with a configurable, mutable `tools/list` response so reconciliation (add/update/deactivate) could be exercised across repeated syncs. Along the way, found and fixed a real bug in `startHttpContractServer`: it reused a single `StreamableHTTPServerTransport` for the server's whole lifetime, which only supports one session — fixed by keying a transport per session, per the SDK's own multi-session pattern.\n\n**Verification**: full build (`pnpm run build`), full test suite (`pnpm run test` — unit + integration + e2e, 562+ tests) and dependency-boundary check (`pnpm run check:boundaries`) all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
